    "notes":  [
                  "All five data-gathering steps completed; see per-field _note entries for source caveats.",
                  "STOOQ CSV ENDPOINTS FAILED: both https://stooq.com/q/d/l/?s=orcl.us\u0026i=d and https://stooq.com/q/d/l/?s=^spx\u0026i=d returned an HTML/JavaScript proof-of-work bot-verification challenge page instead of CSV data (not solvable without executing arbitrary client-side JS to satisfy a SHA-256 proof-of-work challenge, which was treated as bot-detection and not bypassed). As a substitute free public data source, used Yahoo Finance\u0027s public chart JSON endpoint (https://query1.finance.yahoo.com/v8/finance/chart/ORCL?range=3y\u0026interval=1d and analogous %5EGSPC URL), fetched directly via HTTPS on 2026-09-22, and converted to the same Date,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume CSV layout stooq would have produced. Data was cross-validated against FRED\u0027s SP500 series (exact match on 2026-09-21 close: 7764.70) and against stockanalysis.com\u0027s live ORCL quote (exact match on 2026-09-22 close: 149.20), so the substitute source is considered reliable.",
                  "prices_orcl_daily.csv and prices_spx_daily.csv each contain 751 daily rows (plus a 1-row header = 752 lines) spanning 2023-09-25 through 2026-09-22.",
                  "WSJ market-data quotes page (wsj.com) and Google Finance could not be fetched in this tool environment (WSJ blocked outright; Google Finance returned an \u0027unsupported device\u0027 placeholder with no data). stockanalysis.com and FRED were used as the primary public quote sources instead, as permitted by the task\u0027s example source list.",
                  "Oracle\u0027s own IR \u0027Debt Overview\u0027 / fixed income page (investor.oracle.com) was searched for but not located at a specific stable URL via web search in this session; credit ratings were instead sourced from the rating agencies\u0027 own press releases/regulatory filings (S\u0026P Global Ratings site) and reputable financial press (Investing.com, StreetInsider) reporting those releases verbatim with dates.",
                  "Debt instrument table cross-validated internally: sum of all 58 listed instruments\u0027 principal_millions = 130,105, which matches Oracle\u0027s FY2026 10-K disclosed \u0027Total notes payable and other borrowings\u0027 (gross, before unamortized discount of ) of ,105 million exactly (source: R55.htm details table within the same 10-K accession, filing index at https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1341439/000119312526277521/). Current portion of total debt disclosed as ,199M; non-current portion ,342M (net of  unamortized discount/issuance costs, for a net total of ,541M).",
                  "Coupon rates for the 2 floating-rate senior notes (due Aug 2028 and Feb 2029) are reported as their SOFR spread (0.76% and 1.11% respectively), not an all-in rate, consistent with how the 10-K\u0027s \u0027stated interest rate percentage\u0027 field defines them. The Term Loan\u0027s coupon_pct (5.29%) is its FY2026 effective/all-in interest rate (after interest rate swaps), since its base rate is SOFR + 1.35% and an all-in comparable figure is more decision-useful for a board model; the raw SOFR+1.35% spread is noted in its series_name instead.",
                  "Some duplicate-maturity series exist by design per the 10-K (e.g., two separate notes both maturing in May 2030, and both a fixed- and floating-rate tranche maturing in Aug 2028 and again in Feb 2029) -- these are distinct instruments, not data errors."
